<body data-page="admin">
<header class="brandbar"><div class="brandbar-inner">
  <a href="/dashboard" class="mk-logo"><span class="mk-logo-img" role="img" aria-label="Merkle"></span><span class="mk-print-word">Merkle</span></a>
  <span class="mk-sep"></span><span class="mk-title">Analytic Platform Assessment</span>
</div></header>
<div class="subnav">
  <a class="backlink" href="/dashboard">← Dashboard</a>
  <span class="sn-title">Rubric admin · master</span>
  <span class="autosave" id="autosave"><span class="dot"></span><span id="autosaveText">—</span></span>
</div>
<div id="syncBanner" class="sync-banner">
  <span>This rubric was updated by another editor. Reload to pull their changes (your unsaved edits would otherwise overwrite theirs).</span>
  <button class="btn" id="btnSyncReload" style="margin-left:auto;">Reload</button>
</div>
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="readme collapsible" id="rubricReadme">
    <div class="rm-head" data-seccollapse>
      <span class="rm-title">Master rubric — how this works</span>
      <span class="seccaret">▼</span>
    </div>
    <div class="sec-body">
      <p>One rubric powers <strong>every assessment, new and existing</strong>. Edits here apply everywhere; there is no separate save, import, or reset.</p>
      <ul class="rm-list">
        <li><strong>Set support</strong> — click any platform cell to toggle whether that vendor supports the sub-capability (✓ / –).</li>
        <li><strong>Rename &amp; extend</strong> — click a pillar name, capability title, or sub-capability text to edit it; use <em>+ Pillar</em>, <em>+ Capability</em>, and <em>+ Add</em> to extend.</li>
        <li><strong>Retire, don't delete</strong> — pillars, capabilities and sub-capabilities are never deleted. Use <em>Retire</em> to grey out an item so it stops counting in scoring; its data (including SME rationale) is preserved. The same button becomes <em>Unretire</em> to bring it back.</li>
        <li><strong>SME rationale</strong> — click the <span class="pencil">✎</span> on a cell to capture a note, its tone (pro / caveat / note), and your confidence. The ✎ takes on the tone colour once a note is saved.</li>
        <li><strong>Vendors</strong> — <em>+ Add vendor</em> to add a column, drag <span class="drag-handle">⠿</span> to reorder, <em>Retire</em> to archive one (its data is preserved and can be restored).</li>
        <li><strong>Saving</strong> — every change autosaves to the database and syncs live to anyone else editing.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="panel-actions">
    <button class="btn" id="btnExport">Export backup (.json)</button>
    <span class="spacer"></span>
    <button class="btn-add-pillar on" id="addVendorBtn">+ Add vendor</button>
    <button class="btn-add-pillar on" id="addPillarBtn">+ Add pillar</button>
  </div>
  <div class="matrix-key">
    <span class="k"><span class="ck point" style="width:16px;height:16px;font-size:9px">✓</span> Supported</span>
    <span class="k"><span class="ck off" style="width:16px;height:16px;font-size:9px">–</span> Not supported</span>
    <span class="k"><span class="pencil">✎</span> SME rationale — coloured by tone:</span>
    <span class="k"><span class="rat-dot pro"></span> pro · <span class="rat-dot con"></span> caveat · <span class="rat-dot note"></span> note</span>
    <span class="k"><span class="drag-handle">⠿</span> Drag to reorder vendors</span>
  </div>
  <div id="mtxTable" class="mtx-wrap"></div>
  <div id="retiredBar" class="retired-bar"></div>
